---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Flag from '../components/Flag.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="About | Enricco Gemha"
	description="Software engineer from São Paulo, now at Brown. How I got here, and what I’m working on."
>
	<div class="wrapper wrapper-narrow stack gap-12">
		<header class="intro">
			<div class="stack gap-4">
				<h1>About</h1>
				<p class="lede">
					I’m a software engineer from <span class="nowrap">São Paulo <Flag country="br" label="Brazil" /></span>. This is how I got here, and what I’m
					working on now.
				</p>
			</div>
			<img
				src="/assets/portrait.jpg"
				alt="Enricco Gemha, in a navy suit, photographed outdoors in front of evergreen trees."
				width="867"
				height="1200"
				decoding="async"
			/>
		</header>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="how">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="how">How I got here</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					My first code was for my family’s medical accounting office, where I worked in
					high school. Most of the job was paperwork done by hand, so I taught myself
					Python to automate some of it. Then I went to Insper in São Paulo for computer
					engineering.
				</p>
				<p>
					Outside class, I was on a team of four that built two generations of a
					search-and-rescue robot. Our robots won Best in Class for Sensing at RoboCup
					2022 in <span class="nowrap">Bangkok <Flag country="th" label="Thailand" /></span>, and that’s how I became president of the university’s
					robotics and AI club. The next year they won Best in Class for Mapping and Autonomous Navigation at
					RoboCup 2023 in <span class="nowrap">Bordeaux <Flag country="fr" label="France" /></span>. For my capstone I did
					cloud security for <a href="/work/pinpag-capstone/">PinPag</a>, a Brazilian
					payments company, on their live platform.
				</p>
				<p>
					I also took classes for a summer at Stanford and for a semester at Olin and
					Babson, outside Boston. During that semester I started
					<a href="/work/opengiving/">OpenGiving</a> with two American friends: a
					marketplace where part of every sale goes to a fundraising campaign. I wrote all
					of its code, and I’ve been on leave from it since I started at Brown.
				</p>
				<p>
					In September 2025 I joined <a href="/work/zeropunch/">DAERO</a>, a Boston
					startup that makes software for construction crews, as its first engineering hire. The
					first version of their iOS app already existed. I worked on it for ten months,
					and in February 2026 I started rewriting it from scratch. I left in July 2026.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="now">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="now">What I’m doing now</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					I’m doing a master’s in Innovation Management and Entrepreneurship at Brown,
					and I finish in May 2027.
				</p>
				<p>
					I want to get good at security. So far I’ve only done it in school: my capstone,
					and electives on cloud security and offensive tooling. I haven’t found a bug in
					someone else’s system yet. This term I’m taking Systems Security at Harvard,
					and I’m studying for CompTIA Security+.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="tools">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="tools">Tools I reach for</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					<strong>Languages.</strong> Swift, Python, TypeScript, Go, Kotlin, C.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Building.</strong> SwiftUI and WidgetKit, FastAPI, Next.js and Astro,
					Jetpack Compose, PostgreSQL with Prisma, GraphQL, Stripe Connect and PayPal.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Running it.</strong> AWS, Railway, Vercel, GitHub Actions,
					OpenTelemetry and Grafana.
				</p>
				<p>
					<strong>Security.</strong> Semgrep in CI, Wazuh, ModSecurity, and secret
					scanning as a required check.
					<a href="https://www.credly.com/badges/93f53b4d-ed60-47e9-abdd-bc266ec1bf42/public_url" rel="noopener">AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="stack gap-3" aria-labelledby="elsewhere">
			<h2 class="section-label" id="elsewhere">Elsewhere</h2>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					I speak Portuguese and English natively, Spanish well enough to work in, and a
					little Swedish. Outside Brazil and the US, the country I’ve spent the most time
					in is <span class="nowrap">Sweden <Flag country="se" decorative /></span>. I’ve been six times.
				</p>
				<p>I play pickup soccer whenever I can find a game.</p>
				<p>
					Write to me at <a href="mailto:me@enriccogemha.dev">me@enriccogemha.dev</a>,
					or find me on <a href="https://github.com/G3mha" rel="me noopener">GitHub</a>
					and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/enriccogemha" rel="me noopener">LinkedIn</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.intro {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 2rem;
	}

	.lede {
		font-size: var(--text-lg);
		color: var(--ink);
		max-width: var(--measure);
	}

	.intro img {
		width: 100%;
		max-width: 15rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--rule);
	}

	@media (min-width: 42em) {
		.intro {
			flex-direction: row;
			align-items: flex-start;
			justify-content: space-between;
			gap: 3rem;
		}

		/* The portrait stays deliberately small. It is here so a recruiter can put a
		   face to the name, not so it competes with the first paragraph. */
		.intro img {
			flex: none;
			width: 13rem;
		}
	}
</style>
